The resume button is huge. It's inside `.pause-actions` which is flex column. `.pause-actions .btn { width: 100% }`. Button is `display: inline-flex`, min-height 54px. Why huge height? A flex item in column flex container with `alight-items: stretch` default. But there's no `flex: 1` on the primary... Wait `.pause-actions .btn-primary { flex: 1 1 190px; }` — in a column flex container, flex-basis applies to height! So `flex: 1 1 190px` gives primary a basis of 190px height and then it grows to fill remaining free space. That's the bug. Fix: in pause-actions, set `flex: 0 0 auto` for the primary (or `flex: none`). Need width 100%.

Also `.pause-card` text-align center. Let me patch:

```css
.pause-actions .btn-primary {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
}
```

But `.pause-actions .btn` width 100% and min-height. Good.

Also flex-direction column, and there's no set height on .pause-card, so free space shouldn't exist... but wait, `.pause` is `display:grid; place-items:center`, pause-card height auto. So how did the button get huge? flex-basis 190px in column direction → height at least 190px even without free space. Yes that's it. So fix.

